        "id": 1026112
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-21T16:35:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry if I was unclear. It does filter out user refs for anonymous users. There was a bug in this code that was:\n\nif ((accountId \u003d Account.Id.fromRef(refName)) !\u003d null \u0026\u0026 currentUser !\u003d null)\n\nNow this is \nif ((accountId \u003d Account.Id.fromRef(refName)) !\u003d null)\n\nThe check for currentUser !\u003d null prevent that we go into this if for anonumous users once again forcing us to apply normal Gerrit permissions.\n\nThe new checks for different Gerrit refs inside RefControl#hasReadOnRef are just an additional safe guard that would have thrown in this case (which is better than leaking).",
      "parentUuid": "169e7b8d_dc04adbf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 89
      },
